  "title": "Oldenburg 1998 · Gold nanoshell growth · Best fits",
  "description": "Eight nanoshell interpretations from Figures 3a and 3b. Four small-core and four large-core samples retain the fitted lognormal distributions, one shared core population per family, Olmon/McPeak Au and A = 1 with L = 4V/S. The rising 3b trace is interpreted as a thin complete shell with a constant vertical plotting offset. Only its particle model is rendered. All samples use an illustrative 20 mg Au/L, not a concentration inferred from the historical plot. Labels give mean core diameter and mean shell thickness ± shell SD in nm. Core and shell sizes are optical fits rather than independent structural measurements.",
